{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793545856,"nonce":"6tfTXBAzcwRioePp55kmFr+Vgqo=","message":"Resolved 2026-11-01 by a controlled repro (just test chaos pause-node: docker pause of the kind node for 930 s, landed 1.6 s after the producer's step exited). Pod record: the egress sidecar terminated exit 137 at the unpause; the kubelet's terminationGracePeriodSeconds (600 s) for the sidecar ran out during the freeze, so it SIGKILLed it on resume. The 'workspace snapshot lost' verdict is TRUE, not false: the drain never recorded a root and no container is left to drain from. The executor's ceiling is grace + 300 s, so in a whole-node freeze the kubelet always acts first; an executor-side clock fix cannot help (the watch_clock change on the stack is being reverted). The Runs then dead-letter by ADR-0047 policy: Infra never_started:false is retried only on the author's retry: assertion, because the step ran. The original report's 'the egress container was still running when checked' was not reproduced. Closing: not a bug; a host sleep longer than the Pod grace loses that Attempt's snapshot by design.","files":null}]}